{"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGestureResolver","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/GestureShortcuts","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/ZoomStep","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchStepper"],"title":"Gestures and zoom","anchor":"Gestures-and-zoom"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"TrackpadGestures","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireInput"}],"externalID":"s:13HeadwireInput16TrackpadGesturesV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stroke runs from its first touch down to its last touch up. It goes "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"silent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" once three fingers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are down, before any finger has moved "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"type":"text","text":" from where it landed and while no button the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"surface pressed is held (the trackpad’s press-and-hold drag), however slowly they came down and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whatever else rests on the glass. From then until the next stroke’s first touch the surfaces send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it, no pointer motion, click, button or scroll (a tap’s action runs after its touch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has ended, so silence outlasts the last lift). A two-finger scroll that a third finger joins after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moving is never silent and goes on as it always did; a stroke that never has three fingers down is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never silent, so one- and two-finger strokes are exactly what they were."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A silent stroke is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"armed"}]},{"type":"text","text":", one that can become a gesture, when the three fingers that landed last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"came down within "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordWindow"},{"type":"text","text":" of each other, before any finger moved "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"type":"text","text":", with no button"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held, no touch of the stroke cancelled and at most four fingers down. So a thumb resting on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"glass before neither keeps three fingers from arming nor becomes one of them; three fingers placed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slowly are silent and decide nothing."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision comes at the first lift of one of those three (another finger lifting only leaves the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stroke), from their centroid’s net travel since arming, and their spread. A swipe when the centroid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"travelled ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeDistance"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickDistance"},{"text":" while moving at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickSpeed"},{"text":" over the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickWindow"},{"text":"), one axis beats the other by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axisRatio"},{"text":", and the fingers moved together: each of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the three at least ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeShare"},{"text":" of the centroid’s way along the swipe, and no other finger that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moved (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"text":" or more) that share or more against it. In a pinch or a spread some digit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moves against the others, however far the centroid goes (a thumb-led pinch drags it along with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the thumb). Else a pinch or a spread when the mean distance from the centroid changed by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pinchRatio"},{"text":", of the three and every other finger that moved (a thumb pinching with three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingers); else nothing. At most one decision per stroke; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fingers"},{"text":" counts the three and the other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingers that moved, 4 at most. A fifth finger down leaves the stroke silent and deciding nothing;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"touches the system cancels decide nothing. So a swipe taken back before the lift does nothing, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on a Mac, and a four-finger stroke that iPadOS takes for itself (its touches cancelled) never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reaches the Mac.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure: Foundation and CoreGraphics only, covered by "},{"code":"TrackpadGesturesTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Deterministic: the same touches give the same outputs. Main thread, as the touches come."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three- and four-finger strokes on the glass, for the Mac: which stroke is a gesture, and which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture it is. Each input surface feeds one of these with every direct touch, through its stroke"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observer. The counts below say three; with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"type":"text","text":" 4 read four."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/armed","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/chordFingers","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/silent"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/cancelled(_:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/down(_:at:time:holding:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInpu